Third-party software
--------------------
Jot depends on the following open-source packages (via Swift Package
Manager); each remains under its own license:

- FluidInference/FluidAudio — Apache License 2.0
- sindresorhus/KeyboardShortcuts — MIT
- sparkle-project/Sparkle — MIT and permissive component licenses
  (see Sparkle's bundled LICENSE)
- john-rocky/CoreML-LLM — MIT
- mattt/EventSource — MIT
- apple/swift-asn1, swift-atomics, swift-collections, swift-crypto,
  swift-nio, swift-system — Apache License 2.0
- huggingface/swift-huggingface, swift-jinja, swift-transformers —
  Apache License 2.0
- ibireme/yyjson — MIT

Bundled binary (not via Swift Package Manager):

- FFmpeg — LGPL v2.1 or later. Jot bundles a minimal, decode-only,
  network-free build of FFmpeg 7.1.1 (`Contents/Helpers/ffmpeg`) used ONLY
  as a fallback decoder for audio/video containers AVFoundation cannot read
  (WebM, MKV, WMA, AVI, …). It is built with no GPL/nonfree codecs and is
  invoked as a separate executable (not statically linked into Jot's binary),
  so the LGPL relink requirement is satisfied by replacing the binary. The
  full license text and exact build recipe ship in the source at
  `Vendor/ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1` and `Vendor/ffmpeg/BUILD.md`; corresponding
  source is available on request. FFmpeg is a trademark of Fabrice Bellard.

Apache-2.0-licensed components are used unmodified; their license and
any NOTICE files ship with the packages themselves.

Speech models are fetched at runtime by FluidAudio and are covered by
their own upstream licenses (Parakeet: MIT/Apache-2.0).
